<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin of Ibelin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1187</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Baldwin of Ramla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin of Ibelin was a baron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> and Mirabel and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan of Ibelin</a>. He fought in the Christian victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> at Montgisard in 1177. In 1186 he refused to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a> as king, left his lands to his son and went into exile in the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-of-ibelin.jpg" alt="Baldwin of Ibelin" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_maison_d%27Ibelin.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
